---
description: pytest conventions for Python code
globs: **/test_*.py,**/*_test.py,**/tests/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---
- Tests live in `tests/` and use `pytest` (plain `assert`, fixtures, `parametrize`); no `unittest.TestCase`.
- Every numeric assertion states its unit and tolerance (`pytest.approx(x, rel=..., abs=...)`); never compare floats with `==`.
- Use small, fixed fixtures checked into the repo. No network, no wall-clock time, no unseeded randomness.
- Cover edge cases, not just the happy path: empty input, single row, DST transitions, NaNs, boundary values. No cap on test count.
- Don't import private pytest internals (`_pytest.*`).
- A bug fix starts with a failing test that reproduces it.
